Structural Damage & Concrete Crack Detection Model
📖 Overview
This repository contains a trained computer vision model designed to automate the inspection of concrete structures (bridges, buildings, and roads). The goal of this project is to detect and classify various types of structural damage, ranging from natural wear and tear to high-impact damage.
Early detection of these anomalies is crucial for:

Infrastructure Safety: Preventing catastrophic failures in bridges and buildings.

Maintenance Efficiency: Automating the visual inspection process.

Disaster Response: Quickly assessing damage after conflict or natural disasters.

Class Definitions
The model is trained to identify and localize 4 distinct classes of structural damage. The classes are mapped as follows:

Class ID     Class Name          Description                                                     	Severity Level
0	         Bullet_impact	     Specific damage patterns caused by ballistic projectiles.	        🔴 High
1	         Explosion_Impact	 Large-scale structural damage caused by blast forces.	            🔴 Critical
2	         normal_crack	     Minor hairline fractures or surface-level concrete crazing.	    🟡 Low/Monitor
3	         severe_crack	     Deep, widening structural fissures indicating potential failure.	🟠 Medium/High